# Fixed 2026-10-01, defect 140, lane emit: the walks that stopped at a depth.
# Symptom: two walks over a record type were bounded at `depth > 16`, and
# past the bound they said nothing: a map key holding a `ptr` seventeen
# records down was built, and inserting one aborted at run with *entered
# unreachable code — this is a compiler bug*; `==` over values holding a
# union sixteen records down was built and read the union's bytes under two
# types.
# Cause: the bounds cited the checker's partial walk as their model, and
# that walk had been made total by defect 046 on 2026-09-16. Both are total
# and flat now, so the refusal holds at every depth.
# This case: the pointer, at the first depth that was built.

record R0
    p: ptr

record R1
    inner: R0

record R2
    inner: R1

record R3
    inner: R2

record R4
    inner: R3

record R5
    inner: R4

record R6
    inner: R5

record R7
    inner: R6

record R8
    inner: R7

record R9
    inner: R8

record R10
    inner: R9

record R11
    inner: R10

record R12
    inner: R11

record R13
    inner: R12

record R14
    inner: R13

record R15
    inner: R14

record R16
    inner: R15

function main()
    m: {R16: i64} = {}  #~ pointer_element
    print(len(m))
